#hasheq((campaign . "v1.00.24-test-design-hotspot-remediation") (kind . "wave-review") (notes . ("root containment: every discovered path must resolve inside the configured root; symlinked directories and .. components cannot escape it, and a missing root is a deterministic rackunit failure (nonzero runner exit) rather than a silent empty result" "path normalization: discovery returns relative normalized path strings under the active root; fixture-root results are sorted by relative-path bytes so ordering is platform-independent and stable" "default-call compatibility: an omitted root in collect-test-files (and the metadata selection helper) preserves the pre-wave default repository discovery behavior; the unit suite asserts the default result is a superset of the fixture-root results and contains none of the fixture paths" "metadata cache isolation: classification/metadata entries are keyed under the active root, so fixture-root selection cannot observe or be perturbed by live-root metadata and vice versa" "deterministic ordering: fixture-root ordering and shard partitioning are pure functions of the relative paths, and repeated invocations agree" "scope disclosure: the previous attempt failed delivery verification because the W0 fitness test froze the behavior table at 12 IDs while the regenerated ledger and ownership map carried 14; commit 8cac901c updates tests/test-test-gate-ownership.rkt to freeze all 14 IDs including the two W5 rows" "untouched invariants: suite definitions, default collection root, shard algorithm, scheduler, and CI invocation are unchanged; repository-scale discovery left the fast suite only via retier to the L4 smoke, not by weakening the classifier or sharder")) (reviewer . "q-agent-independent-review") (scope . "fixture-root discovery seam in run-tests collector/classifier; hermetic fixture tree; repository-scale L4 discovery smoke; ledger/ownership retier; hotspot after-manifest") (status . "completed") (verdict . "pass") (wave . "W5"))